Tuesday Update
* Trade Alert: SPWR calls exit; AMD calls slippping but in gear. * Stocks c=
hop around after tagging new highs amid renewed economic optimismStocks are=
 logging all-time highs as optimism over the economic recovery continues to=
 ripple through markets worldwide. In contrast, bonds extended the worst st=
art to a year since 2013.The S&amp;P 500, Nasdaq Composite and Dow Jones In=
dustrial Average indexes all set records Tuesday, before easing from the hi=
ghs. The MSCI benchmark for emerging and developed market stocks rose for 1=
2 straight sessions, the longest run of gains in 17 years. In Japan, the Ni=
kkei 225 Stock Average extended its advance past the 30,000 level. European=
 markets were mostly little changed after a rally on Monday.The reflation t=
rade is powering assets tied to economic growth and price pressure, includi=
ng commodities and cyclical stocks. At the same time, investors are riding =
a wave of speculative euphoria from penny stocks to Bitcoin amid abundant p=
olicy support.=E2=80=9CWe certainly have data that suggests that being more=
 glass half full than glass half empty remains the right posture,=E2=80=9D =
said Eric Freedman, chief investment officer at U.S. Bank Wealth Management=
. =E2=80=9CPeople are looking at parts of the world as well as sectors that=
 have been underperforming and saying =E2=80=98hey this is maybe the next p=
art of the market that heads higher.=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D -- BloombergPortfoli=
o: We sold second half of SPWR calls on stop Friday for 11% loss after sell=
ing first half half Feb 11 for 25% gain. =E2=80=A6 AMD calls are struggling=
 but still in gear; adjust targets/stop. =E2=80=A6 PTON calls order did not=
 fill Friday. =E2=80=A6 No new recommendations in choppy conditions.*CURREN=
T RECOMMENDATIONSSunPower Corp. (SPWR) February $48 calls-- Symbol: SPWR210=
219C00048000-- Bought on Feb. 9 at $5.50-- Sold half Feb. 11 at $6.90 targe=
t for 25.4% gain-- Sold second half Friday at $4.90 for 11% loss-- Overall =
gain was 14%*Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) March $95 calls-- Symbol: AMD2103=
19C00095000-- Bought Feb. 10 at $4.70.-- Now trading at $3.85-- Set up to s=
ell half at new $5.35 lmt gtc and half at new $6.15 lmt gtc-- Keep stop at =
$3.55 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanA=
ll recommendations are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of =
the specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 =
a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orders are good for the d=
ay only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close of th=
e current session. Past results are no guarantee of future returns. All acc=
ounts may not achieve comparable results. Recommendations are leveraged and=
 speculative, so only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford=
 to lose. All results are shown ex-commissions and fees. Options trading in=
volves the risk of substantial loss. Some news and research provided by Wal=
l Street Journal, Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nb=
sp;

